canvas; the title, legends, and outlines follow its luminance\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"657c1c65-980e-511d-1303-964f19bb2067"]}
  }]], "3ColumnTableMod",
 CellID->1606118752,ExpressionUUID->"0f15dbd5-5f35-596c-352a-d29f5ac02bb6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The backend and any overrides go together in one list, for example a white \
canvas with the edge thickness driven by the ",
 Cell[BoxData["cz"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e9b7e66-629a-1114-26b9-7040172f607e"],
 " duration:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2141499446,ExpressionUUID->"585a51e6-774f-2dd2-087a-48c002fa7738"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ibm", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<ErrorMap\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<Backend\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<ibm_fez\>\""}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<BackgroundColor\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "White"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<EdgeThicknessMetric\>\"", " ", "->", 
      " ", "\"\<Duration\>\""}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellID->339082558,ExpressionUUID->"1d7c0b5b-c40c-ea6a-4b03-a304edbeb8b0"],

Cell["Why the bonds are bidirectional", "Section",
 CellID->432388834,ExpressionUUID->"370294fd-9e49-2d35-5d31-0da71bfc741f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "IBM's native two-qubit gate is the controlled-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2845529c-454d-b13b-587b-4bc66cf90001"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["CZ",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "=", 
   StyleBox["diag",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "1", ",", "1"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7519012f-e657-215b-2326-988893e273a1"],
 ", which is ",
 StyleBox["symmetric",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": swapping the two qubits leaves the gate unchanged, and the hardware \
calibrates both orderings to identical numbers. There is therefore no control \
or target for a ",
 Cell[BoxData["cz"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "594776df-9e75-d16a-0f7d-6f991b01a3b0"],
 ", which is why the bonds are undirected and the arrows are drawn \
double-headed (bidirectional) rather than one-way."
}], "Text",
 CellID->443736588,ExpressionUUID->"6405505f-4b92-3bd6-0c3b-4a196e24893c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A directional ",
 Cell[BoxData["CNOT"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6878c7f8-419e-9db5-1807-dea27028e79f"],
 " is synthesized from a ",
 Cell[BoxData["cz"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48a3d607-c312-9dd3-7850-c860f6a4e739"],
 " and single-qubit gates, with the basis-change Hadamards placed on \
whichever qubit you choose. So a ",
 Cell[BoxData["CNOT"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "539491e8-328f-8d7b-01ab-08b2473bd441"],
 " can be realized in either orientation on the same physical bond: either \
qubit can serve as control or target."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1593449978,ExpressionUUID->"7fcf59b5-a5ca-2155-25f5-50fecc7f73bf"],

